      "label": "vault_mcp.py PEP 723 header drops the ragmark mcp extra",
      "file": "../plugins/workbench/machinery/engine/vault_mcp.py",
      "oracle": "real",
      "find": "\"ragmark[mcp] @ ",
      "replace": "\"ragmark @ "
    },
    {
      "label": "[control] uv.lock wheel hash is wrong by one digit",
      "file": "../plugins/workbench/machinery/uv.lock",
      "oracle": "real",
      "find": "hash = \"sha256:700e6caf8e5e1356b1725f18b0cbeda3e44c5d137b135441d62a35c61cb75a24\"",
      "replace": "hash = \"sha256:700e6caf8e5e1356b1725f18b0cbeda3e44c5d137b135441d62a35c61cb75a25\"",
      "expect": "survived",
      "why": "Not inert, and no dependency test can see it: each test compares one declaration site (the lock, a manifest, the Makefile) to a constant in the test file, and none of those constants holds the release asset's digest, so nothing can grade the hash. The installer is the guard: uv refuses a wheel whose sha256 differs from the one recorded (checked with `uv pip install --require-hashes` on this wheel, one digit off: exit 1, 'Hash mismatch'). Carried as a control so the gap sits in the executable record: if a test ever pins the digest this row goes control-broken and must be turned into a killing row."
    },
    {
      "label": "[control] Makefile pin comment reworded",
      "file": "../Makefile",
      "oracle": "real",
      "find": "# equals machinery/pyproject.toml's and each engine script's inline one, and",
      "replace": "# matches machinery/pyproject.toml's and each engine script's inline one, and",
      "expect": "survived",
      "why": "A prose comment in the Makefile; make ignores it, and the dependency tests read the MACHINERY_TEST_PYTHON assignment (through `make -n`) and the manifests, not comment text. Inert on every path unless a test greps this comment, in which case the runner reports the control as broken."
    }
